{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Information.ChiMinusSix","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Information.ChiMinusSix","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":18,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.chi_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.chi_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/ChiMinusSix.lean#L95-L100","doc":"**The non-vanishing leg, conditionally (sorry-free).**  In particular\nthe derived obstruction residue is nonzero — the leg that\n`conj:qou-p-neq-np` needs, obtained here as an axiom consequence with\nno computational-complexity input. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.chi_eq_neg_six","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.chi_eq_neg_six","kind":"theorem","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/ChiMinusSix.lean#L87-L93","doc":"**Given a QOU, χ(A) = -6 (sorry-free, conditional).**  Composes the\ntwo `QOUObstruction` inputs: the obstruction equals the Bring Euler\ncharacteristic, and the Bring genus is 4, so `χ(A) = 2 - 2·4 = -6`.\nThe conclusion is scoped to the QOU (the `[QOUObstruction]`\nhypothesis) — it is *not* an unconditional assertion. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.QOUObstruction.chi_eq_eulerChar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.QOUObstruction.chi_eq_eulerChar","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/ChiMinusSix.lean#L85-L85","doc":"**Obstruction reduction** (`prf:qou-obstruction-reduction`):\nRiemann–Roch identifies the rank-one `HH²` scalar with the Bring\nsurface's topological Euler characteristic. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.QOUObstruction.chi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.QOUObstruction.chi","kind":"def","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/ChiMinusSix.lean#L81-L81","doc":"The universal obstruction residue at the substrate (the scalar in\n`HH² ≅ k`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.QOUObstruction.bringGenus_eq_four","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.QOUObstruction.bringGenus_eq_four","kind":"theorem","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/ChiMinusSix.lean#L78-L78","doc":"Bring's curve is a genus-4 Riemann surface. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.QOUObstruction.bringGenus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.QOUObstruction.bringGenus","kind":"def","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/ChiMinusSix.lean#L76-L76","doc":"Genus of the substrate's Bring curve — classically `4`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.QOUObstruction.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.QOUObstruction.mk","kind":"ctor","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/ChiMinusSix.lean#L74-L74","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.QOUObstruction.toQOUCohomology","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.QOUObstruction.toQOUCohomology","kind":"def","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/ChiMinusSix.lean#L74-L85","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.QOUObstruction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.QOUObstruction","kind":"class","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/ChiMinusSix.lean#L69-L85","doc":"**The QOU obstruction data (§3b-cond class).**  Extends the\ncohomological assumptions with the geometric inputs that pin the\nscalar's *value*: the substrate Bring surface (genus 4, icosahedral\n`A₅` geometry) and the Riemann–Roch identification of `χ(A)` with its\nEuler characteristic.  All are *inputs*; the value `-6` is derived. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.obstruction_rank_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.obstruction_rank_one","kind":"theorem","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/ChiMinusSix.lean#L63-L67","doc":"**The obstruction is a single scalar (sorry-free).**  Because\n`HH²(A) ≅ k` is rank one, the universal obstruction class lives in a\none-dimensional space — a single element of `k`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.QOUCohomology.frobeniusHopf_duality","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.QOUCohomology.frobeniusHopf_duality","kind":"theorem","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/ChiMinusSix.lean#L61-L61","doc":"Frobenius–Hopf self-duality: `HH² ≅ k` is rank one. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.QOUCohomology.hh2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.QOUCohomology.hh2","kind":"def","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/ChiMinusSix.lean#L59-L59","doc":"`dim HH²(A)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.QOUCohomology.observability","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.QOUCohomology.observability","kind":"theorem","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/ChiMinusSix.lean#L57-L57","doc":"Observability axiom: `HH⁰` vanishes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.QOUCohomology.hh0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.QOUCohomology.hh0","kind":"def","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/ChiMinusSix.lean#L55-L55","doc":"`dim HH⁰(A)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.QOUCohomology.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.QOUCohomology.mk","kind":"ctor","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/ChiMinusSix.lean#L53-L53","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.QOUCohomology","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.QOUCohomology","kind":"class","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/ChiMinusSix.lean#L37-L61","doc":"**The cohomological assumptions a QOU is built from.**  A QOU's\nobstruction context is fixed by two Hochschild-cohomology facts of\nthe categorical substrate `A`:\n\n* **observability** — the observability axiom kills degree-0\n  obstructions, `HH⁰(A) = 0`; and\n* **Frobenius–Hopf self-duality** — Yekutieli–Van den Bergh Poincaré\n  duality is invoked for `HH²(A) ≅ (HH¹)^∨ ≅ k`, so `HH²` is rank one.\n  (Corrected 2026-09-15: this line read `(HH⁰)^∨`, which with `hh0 = 0`\n  would give `HH² = 0`.  The rank-one claim itself is now the Wigner\n  axiom, `conj:wigner-axiom`, not a consequence of the QOU axioms:\n  at `q = 1` Whitehead's lemma gives `HH²(U(𝔤), M) = 0`; see\n  `docs/audits/2026-09-15-chi-as-a-component-of-the-chern-character.md` §2.4.)\n\nEncoded by their ranks (`hh0 = 0`, `hh2 = 1`); the rank-one `HH²` is\nexactly *why* the universal obstruction is a single scalar. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.eulerChar_four","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.eulerChar_four","kind":"theorem","line":34,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/ChiMinusSix.lean#L34-L35","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.eulerChar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.eulerChar","kind":"def","line":30,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/ChiMinusSix.lean#L30-L32","doc":"The topological Euler characteristic of a genus-`g` orientable\nsurface, `χ = 2 - 2g`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}